course: dictionary
lesson: 5493
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and launch is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «The James Webb Space Telescope, launched on Christmas Day 2021, works about 1.5 million km from Earth.» Telescopes are sent up into space, so launched means sent up into the air or space.
explain: Now check a different clue. «Dad helped us launch the little boat into the lake.» A boat goes into water, so launch here means to put the boat into the water. Try the meaning in the sentence to check it: "Dad helped us send the little boat into the lake" makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Look at the word form too. Launch can be an action word, as in «They will launch the phone on Monday.» It can also be a name for a thing or an event: «A launch is a large motorboat.» Ask yourself: is launch something someone does, or is it a thing?
fact: Launch means to send something up into the air or space, to put a boat into water, or to start something new so people can use it.
fact: «Launch» can also be a noun. A launch is the act of launching, and a launch is also a large motorboat.
fact: «Launched» in «Voyager 1 and Voyager 2, launched in 1977» means sent off into space in 1977.
fact: In computing, to launch an app means to open it.
fact: A launch pad is the place a rocket takes off from.
exercise: «NASA's Dragonfly is due to launch around 2028.» What does launch mean here? | To be put into the water | To be opened on a phone | To be painted in bright colours | *To be sent up into space
exercise: «Dad helped us launch the little boat into the lake.» What does launch mean here? | To sink the boat | To paint the boat | To laugh at | *To put the boat into the water
exercise: «A launch is a large motorboat.» What is a launch in this sentence? | A way of opening an app | A rocket in space | A small wooden spoon | *A large motorboat
test: Tom says, «The company will launch its new phone on Monday.» What does launch mean? | To break it into pieces | *To start it and make it available to the public | To hide it in a box | To sink it in the sea
test: In science, pupils launch paper rockets and measure how far they travel. What are they doing to the rockets? | To folding them into paper boats | *Sending them up into the air | Painting them | Reading them aloud
exam: Which sentence uses launch as a noun, meaning a thing or an event? | «Please launch the app now.» | «Launch the boat slowly.» | *«The launch was a huge success.» | «They will launch the spacecraft tomorrow.»
